# Project Overview

> Onboarding for new LLMs joining this project. Read this AFTER
> AIMemory/INDEX.md (which tells you what files exist) and BEFORE
> AIMemory/work.log tail (which tells you what's happening right now).

## What is this project?

A flashcard learning app for spaced repetition (Leitner + Ebbinghaus model).
iOS/Android via Expo + React Native. Korean UI. JLPT N5 vocabulary bundled
by default; the schema supports user-authored decks for future expansion.

## Tech stack

- Expo SDK 54 + React Native + TypeScript
- expo-sqlite for local persistence (schema v5)
- Zustand for app state (sessionStore, settingsStore)
- expo-notifications for review reminders + quiet hours
- Jest for unit tests; tsc + expo lint for static checks

## Key decisions locked in

- 2026-03-12 (claude-opus-4-5) — SRS state-transition strategy: Option C
  (5 levels: 0=fail, 1=daily, 2=weekly, 3=monthly, 4=mastered). Rationale:
  matches Ebbinghaus + Leitner intuition; level-up immediate on pass,
  level-down to 0 on fail.
- 2026-03-18 (gpt-5-codex review) — Step 3 quiz commits with
  `reviewContextForLevel(level)` not always `'step2'`. Critical P0 fix.
- 2026-04-08 (claude-opus-4-5) — Free Apple Personal Team build path:
  cleared `aps-environment` entitlement, set
  `ENABLE_USER_SCRIPT_SANDBOXING = NO` to avoid RN script issues.
- 2026-04-22 (gemini-2-5-pro proposal, claude-opus-4-5 accept) —
  Memory-tracking dashboard MVP: forgetting curve + at-risk Top 8 +
  recall-by-level calibration. Phase 4 ships.
- 2026-04-26 (gpt-5-codex review, claude-opus-4-5 fix) — TOCTOU race in
  refresh-rotation closed via SELECT FOR UPDATE.

